# The build context is an allow-list: the image is built from pyproject.toml and scripts/ci/requirements.py (its
# dependency list) and wheelhouse/ (the wheel, and the release's constraints when there are any), and from nothing
# else in the checkout. So no state, secret, configuration, build output or source tree can reach an image, and an
# edit anywhere else changes no layer. A file the Dockerfile copies must be named here (a test holds the two equal).
*
!pyproject.toml
!scripts/ci/requirements.py
!wheelhouse
